═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
WHY THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DC Hub aggregates public infrastructure data into one place. Anyone relying on
a number we publish should be able to read the code that produced it, so this
repository is published for READING, AUDIT and REPRODUCTION of our results.

That is a transparency commitment, not a grant of rights. "Source-available"
and "open source" are different things, and this repository is the former.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
1. SOFTWARE — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

No licence is granted to copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense
or sell the software in this repository, or to create derivative works of it.
You may read it, quote it for the purposes of comment, review, audit, security
research or academic study, and run it to verify a published DC Hub result.

Absent this file, a public repository with no licence is already all-rights-
reserved by default. This file does not restrict anything further; it states
the position plainly so nobody has to infer it.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
2. DATA AND PUBLISHED OUTPUTS — A SEPARATE, BROADER GRANT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The data DC Hub publishes is licensed SEPARATELY from this software, and more
permissively. In particular, the DC Hub Power Index (DCPI) — its scores,
verdicts, band thresholds and methodology — is released under
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0), because it is our
own derived analytical work and we want it cited.

Not every data layer carries the same grant. The facility inventory and the
third-party physical layers are composites of upstream sources with their own
terms, and a blanket claim over them would be untrue.

  >>> The authoritative, per-layer statement is DATA-LICENSE.md in this
  >>> repository. Read it before redistributing any DC Hub data.

Where this file and DATA-LICENSE.md appear to conflict about DATA,
DATA-LICENSE.md governs. This file governs the SOFTWARE.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
3. UPSTREAM SOURCES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DC Hub ingests third-party data, some of it under licences with conditions
that pass to anyone who redistributes it further — OpenStreetMap is ODbL 1.0
(attribution AND share-alike). Those obligations are not ours to waive.
DATA-LICENSE.md §4 names every upstream and its terms.

